flowchart TD
    START[Per-Region / Quota-Family<br/>Quota Provisioning] --> DECIDE{Policy decision:<br/>can one governed pool<br/>cover Prod + NonProd/CVAL + DR?}

    DECIDE -->|Yes — DEFAULT<br/>QUA-004 v2.2| PRIMARY
    DECIDE -->|No — narrow EXCEPTION<br/>Azure Quota Group limit<br/>or mandatory Prod-isolation| EXC

    subgraph PRIMARY["PRIMARY MODEL — Single Governed Quota Pool (per region / quota family)"]
      direction TB
      POOL["One pool covers Prod + NonProd/CVAL + DR<br/>allocation by logical earmarks, not physical groups"]
      PF["Earmark: Prod_Reserved_Floor<br/>floor below which Prod quota cannot be reduced<br/>protects production growth buffer"]
      DE["Earmark: DR_Earmark_vCPU<br/>protects DR capacity<br/>= MAX over source portions (max-not-sum, A.6)<br/>NOT the sum of concurrent DR demands"]
      ALLOC["NonProd / CVAL Allocatable Headroom<br/>= Pool Limit − Prod_Reserved_Floor − DR_Earmark_vCPU<br/>also funds quota-neutral emergency transfers"]
      POOL --> PF
      POOL --> DE
      POOL --> ALLOC
    end

    subgraph EXC["EXCEPTION TOPOLOGY — Two Quota Groups (used ONLY when single pool is impossible)"]
      direction TB
      PG["Prod-only Quota Group<br/>Prod CRG quota isolated from NonProd surge"]
      NG["Shared NonProd + DR Quota Group<br/>Effective NonProd Ceiling = Group Limit − DR Floor"]
    end

    PRIMARY --> NEUTRAL["Tier 2 Emergency Transfer is quota-neutral:<br/>NonProd reduction releases quota to the SAME pool<br/>that DR expansion consumes → net change ≈ 0"]
    EXC --> EXCNOTE["Exception rationale: retained only where Azure Quota Group<br/>limits or a governance boundary prevent one pool.<br/>Same earmark semantics apply within the shared group."]

    MAXNOTE["max-not-sum (Appendix D, formula A.6):<br/>DR_Earmark_vCPU = MAX over source DR portions,<br/>because DR events are treated as non-concurrent"]
    DE -.-> MAXNOTE
